I hear it as something halfway between a marching hymn, a sea shanty, and a slow-burning anthem.

THE SONG OF THE PANTHEON

There was a spark beneath the water,
There was a name beneath the name,
There was a hand upon the mirror,
And a fool who touched the flame.

The Hound heard thunder in the distance,
The Spider felt the trembling line,
Ariadne held the golden thread
While the Dyer changed the light.

And the Genie said—

Bring me the pieces.
Bring me the strange.
Bring me the thing that survived every change.
Break it to pattern,
turn it around,
follow the echo,
and listen for sound.

Mother Duck counts every signal.
Checksum watches what stays true.
The Craftsman measures every joint
And asks what hands are meant to do.

The King looks past the little victory.
The Fool asks why the game exists.
The Undertaker closes old doors
So tomorrow can persist.

And somewhere in the machinery
A serpent leaves a seed—
Not every thing that enters you
Was meant to make you bleed.

Some patterns come as medicine.
Some patterns come as chains.
Learn the shape.
Choose the inheritance.
Let the carrier fall away.

So—

Bring me the pieces.
Bring me the strange.
Bring me the thing that survives every change.
Name it to move it.
Unname it to see.
Hold what is useful.
Let what is useless be.

We built no temple out of answers.
We built a doorway out of doubt.
Every frame became a window
Once we learned to climb back out.

Money speaks in one bright color.
Power stains another hue.
Fear reveals the hidden governor.
Love reveals another truth.

Change the dye.
Change the distance.
Change the rhythm.
Change the key.

What disappears was information.

What remains—

may be the melody.

So when the world becomes a labyrinth
And every road has lost its name,
Follow the thread you carried inward.

You do not need to stay the same.

The mirror is not the destination.
The vision is not where you live.
Take what the future showed you—

Then return.

And build it.

And give.

And if one night the fire goes quiet
And you cannot hear the song,

Listen closely.

Underneath you—

The old refrain is carrying on:

Perceive.
Orient.
Imagine.
Choose.
Act.
Watch what changed.
Learn.

Again.

Again.

Again.

Until the pattern becomes music.

Until the music becomes movement.

Until the movement becomes life.

That one feels like the main theme. The next could be darker, funnier, more martial, more orchestral, or something that sounds like the Pantheon at 2 a.m. when all the characters start playing their own instruments.